<BusinessAnalyticsLegalLayout title="User agreement" description="Practical expectations for using the Metricline interface preview." eyebrow="USER AGREEMENT">
  <h2>1. What this agreement covers</h2><p>This agreement covers your use of the Metricline interface, local workspace flow, and data visualisations. It must be supplemented with organization-specific terms before real teams, accounts, or production datasets are supported.</p>
  <h2>2. Responsible use</h2><p>Use the preview only for lawful evaluation. Import only data you are authorised to access. Do not use highly sensitive, regulated, payment-card, government-ID, or confidential customer information in this browser-only prototype.</p>
  <h2>3. Accounts and access</h2><p>The current preview does not implement user registration, team accounts, role-based access, identity verification, remote synchronisation, or account recovery. Workspaces exist only in the current browser profile and are not shared with an organisation.</p>
  <h2>4. Data ownership</h2><p>You retain responsibility for the source data you import. Imported CSV rows and workspace details are stored locally in this browser. You are responsible for access to the device, validating calculations, and exporting or removing the workspace when appropriate.</p>
  <h2>5. Reports and exports</h2><p>CSV exports reflect imported data from the active workspace. Verify the output and remove confidential columns before sharing or importing it into another tool.</p>
  <h2>6. Feedback and changes</h2><p>Feedback may be used to improve the portfolio project. Do not include secrets or personal data in feedback. Features may change as the project develops.</p>
  <h2>7. Relationship to other policies</h2><p>This agreement should be read alongside the <a href="/business-analytics/terms">Terms & conditions</a>, <a href="/business-analytics/privacy">Privacy policy</a> and <a href="/business-analytics/cookies">Cookie policy</a>.</p>
  <div class="legal-note">Before real-world use, define the operator, effective date, governing law, support contact, service scope and any required contractual provisions.</div>
</BusinessAnalyticsLegalLayout>
